00:35:10.500 --> 00:35:14.250
I mean look at the way he set
that up with the red, red cup,

00:35:14.250 --> 00:35:16.297
and it's--

00:35:16.297 --> 00:35:17.880
AUDIENCE: Even the
shape of the plate.

00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:19.585
CHRIS BOEBEL: Yeah,
I know, exactly.

00:35:19.585 --> 00:35:20.085
Yeah.

00:35:24.835 --> 00:35:26.210
CHRISTINE WALLEY:
So this is back

00:35:26.210 --> 00:35:27.752
to one of the older
black and whites.

00:36:36.700 --> 00:36:38.380
So there's tons
of stuff on here.

00:36:38.380 --> 00:36:40.447
We could see a range
of different things

00:36:40.447 --> 00:36:41.780
depending on what your interest.

00:36:41.780 --> 00:36:43.450
Do you want to see
a nuclear blast?

00:36:43.450 --> 00:36:44.500
Do you want to see--

00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:46.270
some of them it's
very interesting,

00:36:46.270 --> 00:36:48.790
it goes back to the very first
stuff that we saw from 1905.

00:36:48.790 --> 00:36:55.300
There's also time lapse
of plants unfolding,

00:36:55.300 --> 00:36:57.920
the same way we saw in
the very early pieces.

00:36:57.920 --> 00:37:01.170
So again, a similar kind of--

00:37:01.170 --> 00:37:03.280
remember back to those
very early pieces

00:37:03.280 --> 00:37:05.380
where they were of
interest to scientists,

00:37:05.380 --> 00:37:08.020
but they were also shown
in public theaters,

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.743
with kind of vaudeville
music in the background.

00:37:10.743 --> 00:37:12.910
So they were meant to be
both popular entertainment.

00:37:12.910 --> 00:37:15.490
And so I mean he's
differently positioned

00:37:15.490 --> 00:37:18.190
with the scientific institution,
but still an interest

00:37:18.190 --> 00:37:21.460
in engaging a broader audience.

00:37:21.460 --> 00:37:24.310
And again, kinds of
images that people--

00:37:24.310 --> 00:37:26.020
that many people found
very fascinating.

00:37:26.020 --> 00:37:30.880
But there's nuclear
explosions, you

00:37:30.880 --> 00:37:33.910
can see him hanging out
with Jacques Cousteau.

00:37:33.910 --> 00:37:36.640
And there's a whole
range of different things

00:37:36.640 --> 00:37:37.390
we can look at.

00:37:37.390 --> 00:37:39.340
Oh, the pigeon is cool.

00:37:39.340 --> 00:37:42.957
I'll do this pigeon one before
